cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research or teaching, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "MIRL Lacuna: a catalogue of an absent archive"
abstract: >-
  A no-build, local-first cataloguer for archives that no longer exist:
  destroyed, damaged, looted, dispersed, and unlocated works recorded with
  evidence hashes, consent states down to the entry, a register of narrators
  whose identities never publish, dated sightings, status histories, loss
  events, typed relations, surviving copies (IIIF), a memorial register, a
  timeline, an atlas of consented places, CSV import, serverless merge,
  fixity checks, passphrase encryption of the working file, and
  self-contained finding-aid and memorial-book exports. Arabic and
  right-to-left ready.
authors:
